 close"},{"text":"த்த","lemma":"tta","gloss":"relative participle"}],"gloss":"kept close"},{"surface":"எறிகல்","parts":[{"text":"எறி","lemma":"eṟi","gloss":"throw"},{"text":"கல்","lemma":"kal","gloss":"stone"}],"gloss":"thrown stone"},{"surface":"போல","parts":[{"text":"போல","lemma":"pōla","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஒளித்த","parts":[{"text":"ஒளி","lemma":"oḷi","gloss":"hide"},{"text":"த்த","lemma":"tta","gloss":"past relative participle"}],"gloss":"hidden"},{"surface":"துப்பினை","parts":[{"text":"துப்பு","lemma":"tuppu","gloss":"strength"},{"text":"இனை","lemma":"iṉai","gloss":"pronominal suffix"}],"gloss":"you who have strength"},{"surface":"ஆதலின்","parts":[{"text":"ஆதல்","lemma":"ātal","gloss":"becoming"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"instrumental"}],"gloss":"therefore"},{"surface":"வெளிப்பட","parts":[{"text":"வெளிப்பட","lemma":"வெளிப்பட","gloss":"clearly"}],"gloss":"clearly","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"யாங்ஙனம்","parts":[{"text":"யாங்ஙனம்","lemma":"yāṅṅaṉam","gloss":"how"}],"gloss":"how"},{"surface":"பாடுவர்","parts":[{"text":"பாடு","lemma":"pāṭu","gloss":"sing"},{"text":"வர்","lemma":"var","gloss":"future third person plural"}],"gloss":"will they sing"},{"surface":"புலவர்","parts":[{"text":"புலவர்","lemma":"pulavar","gloss":"poets"}],"gloss":"poets"},{"surface":"கூம்பொடு","parts":[{"text":"கூம்பு","lemma":"kūmpu","gloss":"mast"},{"text":"ஒடு","lemma":"oṭu","gloss":"sociative case"}],"gloss":"with the mast"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மீப்பாய்","parts":[{"text":"மீ","lemma":"mī","gloss":"top"},{"text":"பாய்","lemma":"pāy","gloss":"sail"}],"gloss":"top sail"},{"surface":"களையாது","parts":[{"text":"களை","lemma":"kaḷai","gloss":"remove"},{"text":"யாது","lemma":"yātu","gloss":"negative verbal participle"}],"gloss":"without lowering"},{"surface":"மிசைப்","parts":[{"text":"மிசைப்","lemma":"மிசைப்","gloss":"on top"}],"gloss":"on top","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பரந்","parts":[{"text":"பரந்","lemma":"பரந்","gloss":"spreading"}],"gloss":"spreading","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தோண்டாது","parts":[{"text":"தோண்டாது","lemma":"தோண்டாது","gloss":"without reducing cargo"}],"gloss":"without reducing cargo","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"புகாஅர்ப்","parts":[{"text":"புகாஅர்ப்","lemma":"புகாஅர்ப்","gloss":"into Puhar port"}],"gloss":"into Puhar port","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"புகுந்த","parts":[{"text":"புகு","lemma":"puku","gloss":"enter"},{"text":"ந்த","lemma":"nta","gloss":"past relative participle"}],"gloss":"entered"},{"surface":"பெருங்கலந்","parts":[{"text":"பெருங்கலந்","lemma":"பெருங்கலந்","gloss":"large ship"}],"gloss":"large ship","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தகாஅர்","parts":[{"text":"தகாஅர்","lemma":"takāar","gloss":"unworthy enemies"}],"gloss":"unworthy enemies"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இடைப்புலப்","parts":[{"text":"இடைப்புலப்","lemma":"இடைப்புலப்","gloss":"middle of the land"}],"gloss":"middle of the land","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பெருவழிச்","parts":[{"text":"பெருவழிச்","lemma":"பெருவழிச்","gloss":"great path"}],"gloss":"great path","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"சொரியும்","parts":[{"text":"சொரி","lemma":"cori","gloss":"spill"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"relative participle"}],"gloss":"spilling"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கடல்பல்","parts":[{"text":"கடல்","lemma":"kaṭal","gloss":"sea"},{"text":"பல்","lemma":"pal","gloss":"many"}],"gloss":"many sea"},{"surface":"தாரத்த","parts":[{"text":"தாரத்த","lemma":"தாரத்த","gloss":"possessing goods"}],"gloss":"possessing goods","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நாடுகிழ","parts":[{"text":"நாடுகிழ","lemma":"நாடுகிழ","gloss":"land"}],"gloss":"land","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வோயே","parts":[{"text":"வோயே","lemma":"வோயே","gloss":"O Lord!"}],"gloss":"O Lord!","split_unverified":true}]}],"literal":"The movement of the red sun / and the orbit of that sun / and the sphere surrounded by that orbit / and the direction in which the wind blows / and the empty sky that exists, saying these / as if they went, measured, and knew, always / there are those who say 'it is of this measure', but all of those / you possess as deep wisdom, and having become of dense actions / like a stone kept in the cheek of a male elephant / you have hidden your strength, therefore, openly / how will poets sing of you? With the mast / without lowering the top sail, without reducing cargo on top, / the large ship that entered Puhar, because of unworthy enemies, / spills its cargo on the great path in the middle of the territory, / O Lord of the land with many riches from the sea!","translation":"There are those who speak with certainty about the movement of the red sun, its path, the celestial sphere surrounding it, the directions of the blowing winds, and the vast empty sky, as if they had traveled there and measured them. Yet, you possess all this knowledge as your innate wisdom, and you perform great deeds while keeping your immense strength hidden, like an elephant holding a stone in its cheek. How then can poets fully sing of your greatness? You are the lord of a land rich with diverse maritime wealth, where large ships enter the port of Puhar with sails fully raised and cargo unreduced, only to spill their abundant goods along the wide roads of the interior to ward off unworthy foes. How can anyone measure your true depth?","modern":"செந்நிறச் சூரியனின் இயக்கத்தையும், அந்தச் சூரியனின் பாதையையும், அதைச் சூழ்ந்துள்ள விண்வெளியையும், காற்று வீசும் திசையையும், வெட்டவெளியான ஆகாயத்தையும் நேரில் சென்று அளந்து அறிந்தவர்களைப் போல, 'இவை இவ்வளவுதான்' என்று வரையறுத்துக் கூறுவோர் உலகத்தில் இருக்கிறார்கள். ஆனால், நீயோ அந்த அறிவையெல்லாம் உனக்குள் செறிவாகக் கொண்டு, ஆண் யானை தன் கவளத்தில் மறைத்து வைத்துள்ள கல்லைப் போல உனது பேராற்றலை வெளியே காட்டாமல் மறைத்து வைத்துள்ளாய். கடல் வழியாகப் பலவகையான பண்டங்களைக் கொண்டுவரும் பெரிய கப்பல்கள், புகார்த் துறைமுகத்திற்குள் நுழையும்போது பாய்களைச் சுருக்காமலும், சுமையைக் குறைக்காமலும் நேரே வந்து, பகைவர்களின் இடைமறிப்பால் நாட்டின் நடுவே உள்ள பெருவழிகளில் அச்செல்வங்களைச் சொரிந்து செல்லும் வளமிக்க நாட்டுக்குத் தலைவனே! இத்தகைய ஆற்றல் கொண்ட உன்னை புலவர்கள் எவ்வாறு முழுமையாகப் பாடி முடிப்பார்கள்?","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Pāṭāṇ tiṇai (praising a king's virtues) and is addressed to the Chola king Nalaṅkiḷḷi by the poet Uṟaiyūr Mutukaṇṇaṉ Cāttaṉār. The poet praises the king's profound wisdom and hidden strength, comparing his quiet power to an elephant that holds a stone in its jaw, ready to strike but keeping it concealed. While scholars claim to measure the vastness of the cosmos—the sun's path, the wind's direction, and the empty sky—the king's true depth remains immeasurable. The poem vividly describes the wealth of the Chola port of Puhar, where massive merchant ships arrive fully laden without even lowering their sails, and their abundant goods are distributed along the inland highways. Through these grand images of the cosmos and the bustling ocean trade, the poet illustrates that the king's greatness and strategic capability are beyond the reach of ordinary praise.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.78],[0.84,0.9],[0.9,1.4],[1.4,1.52],[1.52,1.9],[1.9,2.2],[2.2,2.9],[2.9,3.8],[3.8,3.89],[3.89,4.1],[4.1,5.3],[5.3,5.4],[5.4,5.8],[5.8,7.0],[7.0,7.1],[7.1,7.5],[7.5,8.3],[8.3,9.2],[9.2,9.4],[9.4,9.9],[9.9,10.2],[10.2,11.2],[11.2,11.5],[11.5,12.0],[12.0,12.6],[12.6,13.6],[13.6,14.1],[14.1,14.3],[14.3,14.6],[15.72,16.32],[16.32,17.02],[17.02,17.22],[17.22,17.42],[17.42,17.82],[17.95,18.22],[18.22,18.42],[18.42,19.4],[19.52,20.52],[20.52,21.02],[21.02,21.32],[21.32,21.82],[21.82,21.92],[21.92,23.22],[23.22,23.52],[23.52,23.89],[23.89,24.62],[24.62,24.62],[24.62,24.62],[24.62,24.62],[24.62,24.62],[24.62,27.46],[27.82,28.42],[28.42,28.92],[28.92,29.67],[29.67,30.12],[30.12,30.55],[30.55,30.72]],"female":[[0.0,0.32],[0.32,0.7],[0.7,1.4],[1.4,1.54],[1.54,2.0],[2.0,2.3],[2.3,3.1],[3.1,4.1],[4.1,4.25],[4.25,4.6],[4.6,5.8],[5.8,6.0],[6.0,6.4],[6.4,7.9],[7.9,7.9],[7.9,8.